      "writtenOn": "2013-06-10T18:34:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) is not an issue.  That would be a poorly written plugin.\n\n2) No.  Nothing goes in the log unless there is something to report. Written like the above, it just gets called and returns.\n\n3) again, that is a plugin design call.  Actually, the validation of the ddata is part of the iterative loop right now, but it probably should be pulled into the plugin.  However, that change could happen later.\n\n4) Not under normal circumstances.  Only a plugin written to be executed on all data would do that, and it would be a deliberate decision on the part of the writer and deployer to do so.  As written, we could actually remove the REMOTE_USER code from the plugin pipeline.  The code in master does not allow that.\n\n5) We can\u0027t do that under the existing code, either.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAPX//16Y\u003d",
      "revId": "bf00ba0b43b1e33d7bac0f8fb01113258a5720f1",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
